{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "On-device regression matrix for the webOS Plex player. Each case drives the app headless via /tmp/plxnative-* triggers (see README) and asserts on /tmp/plxnative-events.log. rks are real PMS items (192.168.0.3:32400). The runner (run.py) reads the X-Plex-Token from src/config.local.h at runtime \u2014 it is NEVER stored here. Cases are derived from the library survey; see library_gaps for combos no real item can cover.",
  "pms": {
    "host": "192.168.0.3",
    "port": 32400
  },
  "_test_user_comment": "By default the harness runs as this Plex Home managed user so test playback + timeline scrobbles land on THIS user's history, never the owner's real account. run.py fetches this user's per-server accessToken via the admin token (shared_servers) at runtime -- no secret is stored. Pass --owner to run as the config.local.h owner token instead. The user must already have library access shared (Guest here already does).",
  "test_user": {
    "id": 762808621,
    "title": "Guest"
  },
  "tv": "192.168.0.114",
  "_fps_comment": "On-device UI framerate regression scenes (./tests/run.py --fps, or --fps-player to add the player tier). Each sets its plxnative-* triggers, runs profiler-OFF, parses the FPS= heartbeat for its route(+overlay), skips warmup_s samples, and requires the 2nd-lowest steady FPS >= floor. rk fields are library-specific like the cases below; detail-transition needs an in-home-catalog (recently-added/on-deck) movie or it FAILs with 'never entered route=detail'. NOTE (who's-watching): a multi-user Plex Home roster boots to the who's-watching PICKER (route=profiles), so any home/detail scene MUST set at least one non-diagnostic plxnative-* trigger \u2014 that marks the boot automated and skips the picker to land on route=home. home-hero uses plxnative-heroidx (pins the rotating hero, stays on the hero, no grid snap); home-grid uses plxnative-grid (snaps into the grid). A scene with empty triggers stalls on the picker and FAILs with 'never entered route=home'.",
  "fps_scenes": [
    {
      "name": "home-hero",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "home",
      "floor": 50,
      "run_secs": 18,
      "warmup_s": 5,
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-heroidx": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "home-grid",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "home",
      "floor": 50,
      "run_secs": 18,
      "warmup_s": 5,
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-grid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "detail-transition",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "detail",
      "floor": 45,
      "run_secs": 22,
      "warmup_s": 6,
      "rk": "2012",
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-detail": "$rk",
        "plxnative-detailosc": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "item-menu",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "itemmenu",
      "_floor_note": "45 like the other scrim'd-popover scenes (track-menu, library-switch): this one draws a full-screen scrim plus a panel OVER the live home grid, which is strictly more fill than home-grid's 50.",
      "floor": 45,
      "run_secs": 18,
      "warmup_s": 6,
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-itemmenu": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "person-page",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "person",
      "floor": 50,
      "run_secs": 20,
      "warmup_s": 6,
      "rk": "2005",
      "comment": "cast[0] of this movie is Peter Sallis, who has titles in BOTH libraries, so the page draws two poster shelves. detailsec=1 walks the hero focus down to the credits row (a movie's second section); detailok presses OK on it.",
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-detail": "$rk",
        "plxnative-detailsec": 1,
        "plxnative-detailok": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "library-scroll",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "library",
      "floor": 50,
      "run_secs": 18,
      "warmup_s": 5,
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-library": true,
        "plxnative-libosc": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "library-switch",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "library",
      "floor": 45,
      "run_secs": 22,
      "warmup_s": 6,
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-library": true,
        "plxnative-libswitch": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "home-library-nav",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "home",
      "_floor_note": "45 like library-switch: this is that scene's machinery one altitude up \u2014 a whole-screen cascade alpha over Home's backdrop+hero+grid for ~225ms per bounce, plus the same Xfade underneath. No new pass and no new blending (Painter::c already multiplies every colour), so 45 is the popover/re-query tier, not a new one.",
      "floor": 45,
      "run_secs": 36,
      "warmup_s": 6,
      "_run_secs_note": "36, not the 22 every single-route scene uses, because a ROUTE-CHANGING scene splits its samples. The FPS heartbeat is once/sec and navosc bounces every 1400ms, so each route sees only about HALF the post-warmup samples — 22s gave route=home 4, one under the harness' >=5 minimum, and the scene failed for want of evidence rather than for want of frames. 36s leaves ~30 post-warmup seconds, ~15 per route: margin enough that an uneven bounce phase cannot starve either side. Any future two-route scene needs this same doubling.",
      "comment": "One of the two scenes that change ROUTE. navosc bounces Home<->the first library section every 1400ms through the real nav_to path, so the page cross-fade (ui::nav) is perf-gated. route=home samples the settled hero, the fade-OUT and the fade-IN on the way back; the Library half is covered by library-scroll/library-switch.",
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-navosc": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "home-detail-nav",
      "tier": "ui",
      "route": "detail",
      "_floor_note": "45, the detail tier: this is detail-transition's screen with a whole-screen cascade alpha over it for ~225ms per bounce, and the detail page is the heaviest thing the dip has to carry (full-bleed hero art + the AmbientWash ground + the below-hero flow). No new pass and no new blending — Painter::c already multiplies every colour and the wash mixes toward SURFACE_APP under the same alpha — so it stays that tier rather than opening a new one.",
      "floor": 45,
      "run_secs": 36,
      "warmup_s": 6,
      "_run_secs_note": "36 for the same reason as home-library-nav: a route-CHANGING scene splits its once/sec samples between two routes. This one scraped through at 22s with exactly 6 post-warmup samples against a minimum of 5 — passing on one sample of margin is not a gate, it is a coin flip.",
      "rk": "2012",
      "comment": "The Home<->DETAIL arm of the route transition (phase 2), the half home-library-nav cannot reach: no shared tab bar (so the top band fades WITH the page instead of holding still), a hero backdrop and an ambient ground on the far side, and a real teardown at the fade floor. navosc with a ratingKey bounces nav_open out and nav_back home every 1400ms through the same calls a grid-card OK and the BACK key raise. route=detail samples the arrival ramp, the settled page and the fade-OUT; the Home side is covered by home-hero/home-grid/home-library-nav.",
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-navosc": "$rk"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "info-panel",
      "tier": "player",
      "route": "player",
      "overlay": "info",
      "floor": 45,
      "run_secs": 26,
      "warmup_s": 9,
      "rk": "1926",
      "triggers": {
        "plxnative-play": "$rk",
        "plxnative-info": true
      }
    },
    {
